> alone backup tape, which is all you need to do a VMS installation.
> 
>     -Ken

You're right of course, Ken, about the VAX 6xxx booting from TK70s.

I apologize for creating an unintended trivia storm on booting.
I probably should have simply warned "henk1968" that he needed to
make sure he had boot code to support any tape drive of interest
before he took the effort to create a bootable tape.

Many VAXen (and other systems as well) are pretty limited in what
they will directly boot from.  The VAX 82x0/83x0, for example,
directly booted from the built-in RX50, and the secondary bootstrap
code on that RX50 then knew how to boot from a few "favored" tapes
(TU80, TU81) via a few "favored" datapaths.  A pretty common question
from customers was "How come I can't boot from Tape-X on VAX-Y, since
I can boot from Tape-X on VAX-Z?" -- and there was never an answer
that satisfied them.
-- 
Cheers, Bob


