not open for others.

EMULEX once did a reverse engineering of LAT called ELT, and included it
in the terminal servers they sold (Performance 4000, NetQUE, NetJET, ...)
while Meridian Technology (sp?) did license the protocol itself from DEC
and wrote some products (eg. SuperLAT for Windows-NT) and did sell them
and even did license them to others (IIRC XYPLEX, XCD, LANTRONIX, ...)

Last I heard, they are no longer in this business. Most likely because
the need for (buying) LAT (products) is now virtually nil.

