Forget the MMJ connections, as they're not used for booting or printing.

> I am running Windows XP with an RJ45 network and I am trying to work
> out if I will be able to get this set up to run with the printer.

Connect the appropriate adapter to the BNC network port to connect it
to your network.

I said the printer can boot from Windows, but since the software to do
that has not been maintained since 1998 or so, it has no knowledge of
Windows XP and I've been told it does not work there.

> Or is there a way to do a test print to see if it even still works?

You need to boot the printer first before it will even print its
powerup page.

> It is missing one paper tray does it need both or can I get a way with one?

That's a good question that I don't know off the top of my head.

PrintServer Software is available at this page:

<http://www.compaq.com/products/printers/software/prt_swdrv_printserver.
html>

except for the OpenVMS version, which is available on the quarterly
Software Product Library CDs, among other places.

