Indeed , I would like to use a Postscript printer over USB.

Consider the following:

1. Laser and Inkjet printers get cheaper all the time, but the network 
variants are still relatively expensive. Sometimes you need a seperate 
expensive printserver. (hobbiest would like to print to :-)  ).
2. There is a trend towards Postscript. All HP laser printers (except 
the cheapest pure Windows printers) have Postscript now as a standard 
feature. It used to be a rather expensive option. PCL is at its end it 
seems.
3. Serial and parallel connections are superseded by USB, many new 
printers don't even have a parallel connector anymore.
4. DCPS did support serial connections, so migrating to USB is a natural 
way to go.
5. There is printer support in the new USB drivers for VMS 7.3-1 I have 
been told.

Regards,

Dirk Munk





