I think you need to be a little bit more exact.

I don't think that a VAX 4000 model 100A was ever called MicroVAX, but 
what's in a name? What is a "control microvax"?

The console connector of the VAX 4000-100A is a MMJ socket, not a DB25 
connector.

I don't think any VAX has female (DB25F) connectors as serial ports.

MMJ is a modified RJ12, not a RJ11.

For the information you are looking for, have a look at 
http://www.openvms.compaq.com/wizard/openvms_faq.html#WIRES1

HTH,

