In article <Xns9214DC2EFC7EBjde59@204.118.133.26>,
Jake  <jde59_nospam@yahoo.com> wrote:
> Basically I need to transfer a data file (Simulation Library) from the UNIX 
> based system to the VMS based system.  Does anyone have any helpful 
> suggestions or know of any software applications that will allow me to port 
> the file over?

You note in another message that the systems are not networked, but that you
have a PC that can be used to communicate to both.

I would suggest that you install the Kermit terminal emulator and file
transfer software on all three systems. Kermit was designed for this kind
of situation, and is really the premier non-network file transfer protocol.

If you can connect the systems directly together via a serial line, then
you can use kermit to transfer the file directly. If not, then you can use
the third system connected to each in turn to transfer the file.

You can get Kermit at http://www.columbia.edu/kermit/ .

