Well,

It's been years since I 've done this, but if you are licensed for DECnet
you could bring that up over a serial link between the machines and thus
transfer the data you want with a simple copy.

The kermit way is one angle, a second could be to implement, ZMODEM on each
machine, http://www.omen.com/rzsz.html

A serial cable interconnects them, you start a file xmit on one and a file
rcv on the other and you get a data moved at a reasonable speed with error
checking and recovery to boot.

