21:16:20 GMT:
> >Hi, I own a Digital AlphaServer 1000 and can't even get her to power on
> >anymore.  Should I suspect a power supply problem or are there other
> >things that might cause this?
> >
> >.... the machine also appears to have SCSI controller problems, but one
> >crisis at a time.  ;)
>
> I never had a 1000, but I've done a lot to 2100s.  They insist on having
> their original network/SCSI card installed (which also holds the firmware,
I
> believe).  If that's not there, it won't power up.  If you put in an
> unsupported card, it might not power up.

Nope. 1000s are nothing like 2100s. Everything is on the motherboard, there
is no network/SCSI daughterboard like in the 2100.

The most likely cause is the cover interlock switch on the top. It's in the
center between the two 5.25 drive bays. The spring-loaded clip that actuates
the switch breaks easily. The tab on the top cover that pushes on the switch
can also get bent and not contact the switch. You should also check the
wiring, it's fragile.

Mark Levy
SMA





