> If your Infoserver is connected on your network, try:
>
> $ @SYS$STARTUP:ESS$STARTUP DISK
> $ MCR ESS$LADCP
> LADCP Version X-7
> LASTPort Disk (LAD) Version V3.0
> ESS$DADDRIVER Ident X-21
> LADCP> SHOW SERVICES
>
>
>
> Also, assuming you've started LAT, try:
>
> $ MCR LATCP
> LATCP> SHOW SERVICE
>
> Look for a service that might be your InforServer.  If the Infoserver does
> not have a name assigned to it, it will appear with a name containing the
> ehternet address.
