I am not sure about the 2100, but a RJ11 plug won't fit in a 3100 unless 
you use brute force and in that case it is still not likely to work. You 
need a MMJ plug, which is a modified RJ12.

By the way, this is exactly the same on a DEC3000-400. Also, both the 
3100 and the 3000-400 have a S3 switch, which controls whether the 
console comes up on the graphics head or on the serial port.

HTH,

Bart Zorn



