The "VS3100 Maintenance Guide" (EK-285AA-MG-001) says, on p Testing-4:
"The test number of each device is listed on the power-up screen
display as the device is tested." and on p Testing-5 that the ellipsis
... means: "Device tested successfully or it may have a soft error".

I take this to mean that your machine is stuck in test B = memory;
test A is the Memory Management Unit. Memory testing does sometimes
take a minute or so, but I guess you waited longer than that. The
manual doesn't say what to do if the machine gets stuck in one of the
tests, but I suppose you could try pressing the Halt button. I'd
rather not shut down my 3100 here just to see if that works. What is
the state of the LEDs?

