The old Trio64/2MB card from MIRO (22D, I think) I stuffed into a PC164
board had 'almost' no problems with 1280/x1024@72Hz. I have a slight
moiree effect with the usual 'weave' background from the X server, but
that's quite normal. And yes, VMS 7.2. 
An ATI Mach64 was far worse, very unstable and jittery at anything more
than 1024x768@72Hz.

